# Cloudflare Workers Static Assets: response headers for docs/.
#
# Every browser-fetched .js and .css is `?v=`-stamped by the pipeline
# (pipeline/stamping.py), and the fonts are fixed subsets, so those files are
# immutable: a new build is a new URL. sw.js is fetched by the browser at its
# bare path and must never be cached, or an old worker keeps serving its old
# precache. HTML, manifest.json and the JSON endpoints keep the platform
# default (public, max-age=0, must-revalidate, with an ETag).
#
# Any new browser-fetched .js or .css must be stamped (STAMPED_SCRIPTS or
# STAMPED_DATA) or get its own no-cache rule like sw.js.

/*.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/*.css
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/fonts/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/sw.js
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/icons/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=()
